USB_Host_Shield_Library_2.0 changes for RP2040-Zero / ARPnMIDI.
Only FILE 1 (UsbCore.h) is a functional change. FILE 2 (usbhost.h) is left at the
stock MISO=P0 value — see the note there.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FILE 1: UsbCore.h — declares CS and INT pin numbers for the MAX3421E
Library path: ~/Documents/Arduino/libraries/USB_Host_Shield_Library_2.0/UsbCore.h
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--- a/USB_Host_Shield_Library_2.0/UsbCore.h
+++ b/USB_Host_Shield_Library_2.0/UsbCore.h
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@
 #elif defined(MIGHTYCORE)
 typedef MAX3421e<Pb4, Pb3> MAX3421E; // MightyCore
+#elif defined(ARDUINO_ARCH_RP2040)
+typedef MAX3421e<P1, P26> MAX3421E; // ARPnMIDI MAX3421E-secondary build: CS GP1, INT GP26
 #elif (defined(__AVR_ATmega644P__) || defined(__AVR_ATmega1284P__))
 typedef MAX3421e<Pb4, Pb3> MAX3421E; // Sanguino
 #else

To revert: remove the two +#elif defined(ARDUINO_ARCH_RP2040) lines.
To re-apply after a library update: add them back between MightyCore and AVR ATmega644P.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FILE 2: usbhost.h — SPI pin roles for the spi<> template (NON-functional / stock)
Library path: ~/Documents/Arduino/libraries/USB_Host_Shield_Library_2.0/usbhost.h
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Current RP2040 line (MISO = P0 = GP0, matches the ARPnMIDI PCB and stock value):
  typedef SPi< P2, P3, P0, P1 > spi;  // SCK=GP2, MOSI=GP3, MISO=GP0, SS=GP1

NOTE: On RP2040 with SPI_HAS_TRANSACTION, ONLY the SS pin (P1 = GP1) from this
typedef matters at runtime — MISO/MOSI/SCK come from the Arduino SPI object via
SPI.setRX()/setTX()/setSCK() in each sketch. So this line is documentation only;
no functional patch is needed here. (During bring-up it was briefly set to P4
while we mistakenly believed MISO had to be GP4; it is back to the correct GP0.)
